controlled run: builds the SAME env the live dispatch spawn path builds
(dispatch.scrubbed_env -> adapter.child_env -> the credential allowlist),
then prints KEY NAMES ONLY. No secret value is ever printed.

harness=pi-local  adapter=pi  provider=local-town  credential='none'  needs_credential=False
  OPENROUTER_API_KEY present: False
  key names containing OPENROUTER: []
  key names containing KEY/TOKEN: ['CLAUDE_CODE_MESSAGING_TOKEN']

harness=pi  adapter=pi  provider=openrouter  credential=None  needs_credential=True
  OPENROUTER_API_KEY present: True
  key names containing OPENROUTER: ['OPENROUTER_API_KEY']
  key names containing KEY/TOKEN: ['CLAUDE_CODE_MESSAGING_TOKEN', 'OPENROUTER_API_KEY']

NOTE: the dispatcher process env carries its own inherited
OPENROUTER_API_KEY, which is why the allowlist must DROP it for a
credential-none harness rather than merely skip minting a new one.
